{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 475734, "name": "jrt", "username": "jrtberlin", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/603e79/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-02-02T21:35:53.922Z", "cooked": "<p>Hi, I noticed that systemd on fedora (at least on the atomic variants) is compiled without support for <a href=\"https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/journald.conf.html#Seal=\"><em>forward secure sealing</em> (fss)</a>. This is a systemd feature to detect journal tampering and <a href=\"https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/journalctl.html#Forward%20Secure%20Sealing%20(FSS)%20Options\">verifying the integrity</a>. Any idea why this is turned off or where to propose turning it on in-case there isn’t a reason for it being off?</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2026-02-03T11:32:02.286Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 100, "reads": 42, "readers_count": 41, "score": 508.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 180492, "topic_slug": "systemd-journal-forward-secure-sealing", "display_username": "jrt", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 3, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/journald.conf.html#Seal=", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "clicks": 7}, {"url": "https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/journalctl.html#Forward%20Secure%20Sealing%20(FSS)%20Options", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 31999, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/systemd-journal-forward-secure-sealing/180492/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 475797, "name": "Petr Sklenar", "username": "psklenar", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/psklenar/{size}/52803_2.png", "created_at": "2026-02-03T09:47:44.233Z", "cooked": "<p>Hi,</p>\n<p>the same at ‘normal fedora“ :</p>\n<p><code>❯ journalctl --setup-keys</code><br>\n<code>Compiled without forward-secure sealing support.</code></p>\n<p>systemd is compiled WITHOUT gcrypt which is needed by fss.</p>\n<p><em>I’m hoping you will not ask me why its not compiled with</em> this ^ - <em>I honestly don’t know.</em></p>\n<p>found:</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox githubissue\" data-onebox-src=\"https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/40073\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/40073\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">github.com/systemd/systemd</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"github-row\">\n  <div class=\"github-icon-container\" title=\"Issue\" data-github-private-repo=\"false\">\n\t  <svg width=\"60\" height=\"60\" class=\"github-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 14 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M7 2.3c3.14 0 5.7 2.56 5.7 5.7s-2.56 5.7-5.7 5.7A5.71 5.71 0 0 1 1.3 8c0-3.14 2.56-5.7 5.7-5.7zM7 1C3.14 1 0 4.14 0 8s3.14 7 7 7 7-3.14 7-7-3.14-7-7-7zm1 3H6v5h2V4zm0 6H6v2h2v-2z\"></path></svg>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"github-info-container\">\n    <h4>\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/40073\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">State of forward secure sealing</a>\n    </h4>\n\n    <div class=\"github-info\">\n      <div class=\"date\">\n        opened <span class=\"discourse-local-date\" data-format=\"ll\" data-date=\"2025-12-12\" data-time=\"18:31:28\" data-timezone=\"UTC\">06:31PM - 12 Dec 25 UTC</span>\n      </div>\n\n\n      <div class=\"user\">\n        <a href=\"https://github.com/doggo-premium\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n          <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/7/6/76c4140527e89dc6d22cc2fd44a72fb683b6a23e.png\" class=\"onebox-avatar-inline\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" data-dominant-color=\"EEE6E0\">\n          doggo-premium\n        </a>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"labels\">\n        <span style=\"display:inline-block;margin-top:2px;background-color: #B8B8B8;padding: 2px;border-radius: 4px;color: #fff;margin-left: 3px;\">\n          journal\n        </span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n  <div class=\"github-row\">\n    <p class=\"github-body-container\">Is sealing/verification still supported in current versions? Is support in the f<span class=\"show-more-container\"><a href=\"\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"show-more\">…</a></span><span class=\"excerpt hidden\">uture planned with maybe other crypto libraries?\n\nUsing Fedora 43 with systemd 258.2 gives \"Compiled without forward-secure sealing support\" when trying to run \"journalctl --setup-keys\".\nIt looks like gcrypt is required for that but the version was compiled without gcrypt support.\nLooking at the systemd News gcrypt has been deprecated in general recently. I could not find anything regarding FSS.\nFrom the error message I guess openssl does not support this feature.</span></p>\n  </div>\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2026-02-03T10:14:20.132Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 2, "reads": 37, "readers_count": 36, "score": 22.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 180492, "topic_slug": "systemd-journal-forward-secure-sealing", "display_username": "Petr Sklenar", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 3, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://github.com/systemd/systemd/issues/40073", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "State of forward secure sealing · Issue #40073 · systemd/systemd · GitHub", "clicks": 15}], "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 29818, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/systemd-journal-forward-secure-sealing/180492/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 475855, "name": "Michael Catanzaro", "username": "catanzaro", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/f5a326/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-02-03T15:07:59.402Z", "cooked": "<p>libgcrypt is strongly disfavored, so I’m not surprised to see it disabled wherever possible. Often it’s better to depend on OpenSSL instead.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2026-02-03T15:07:59.402Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 2, "reads": 34, "readers_count": 33, "score": 16.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 180492, "topic_slug": "systemd-journal-forward-secure-sealing", "display_username": "Michael Catanzaro", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 29818, "username": "psklenar", "name": "Petr Sklenar", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/psklenar/{size}/52803_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 2242, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/systemd-journal-forward-secure-sealing/180492/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 475917, "name": "Daniel Milnes", "username": "thebeanogamer", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/thebeanogamer/{size}/30968_2.png", "created_at": "2026-02-03T22:51:38.582Z", "cooked": "<p>The commit responsible for turning it off is <a href=\"https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/systemd/c/ee5cf7fbad21ec37cb20856c381e90479cc4878d?branch=rawhide\">this one</a>. Removing the dependency on libgcrypt apparently significantly simplifies the dependency tree for systemd.</p>\n<p>Out of curiosity I’ve reverted that commit and built in <a href=\"https://copr.fedorainfracloud.org/coprs/thebeanogamer/systemd-fss/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">COPR</a>. It appears to still work but I think I’m in agreement with the others that the feature doesn’t justify reintroducing the dependency.</p>\n<p>I’ll drop a comment on that GitHub post clarifying what’s happened, but I think we wont be able to re-enable this feature until it’s moved over to OpenSSL.</p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2026-02-03T22:51:38.582Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 25, "readers_count": 24, "score": 40.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 180492, "topic_slug": "systemd-journal-forward-secure-sealing", "display_username": "Daniel Milnes", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/systemd/c/ee5cf7fbad21ec37cb20856c381e90479cc4878d?branch=rawhide", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Making sure you're not a bot!", "clicks": 10}, {"url": "https://copr.fedorainfracloud.org/coprs/thebeanogamer/systemd-fss/", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Making sure you're not a bot!", "clicks": 1}], "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 2}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 16638, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/systemd-journal-forward-secure-sealing/180492/6", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 2}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 475921, "name": "jrt", "username": "jrtberlin", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/603e79/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-02-03T23:02:20.583Z", "cooked": "<p>Thank you for the details!<br>\nI don’t think either it’s worth it to introduce that dependency again. Lets hope it gets moved over to openssl at some point.</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2026-02-03T23:02:20.583Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 6, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 4, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 39.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 180492, "topic_slug": "systemd-journal-forward-secure-sealing", "display_username": "jrt", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 16638, "username": "thebeanogamer", "name": "Daniel Milnes", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/thebeanogamer/{size}/30968_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 31999, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/systemd-journal-forward-secure-sealing/180492/7", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}], "stream": [475734, 475797, 475855, 475917, 475921]}, "timeline_lookup": [[1, 274], [4, 273]], "suggested_topics": [], "tags": [{"id": 283, "name": "silverblue-team", "slug": "sil